      ":question/id": "f1af35fb-b2b0-5cb4-a135-e9384056e7e2",
      ":question/problem": "$15{\\left(\\frac{1}{6}\\right)}^{3}=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "To raise the fraction to the power of $3$, we must raise both the numerator and the denominator to the power of $3.$ So we have\n\n$$\n{\\left(\\frac{1}{6}\\right)}^{3}=\\frac{{1}^{3}}{{6}^{3}}=\\frac{1}{216}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n15{\\left(\\frac{1}{6}\\right)}^{3}=15\\cdot \\frac{1}{216}=\\frac{15}{216}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we simplify:\n\n$$\n\\frac{15}{216}=\\frac{5\\cdot 3}{72\\cdot 3}=\\frac{5}{72}\n$$",
