      ":question/problem": "${\\left(-\\frac{3}{5}\\right)}^{2}=$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that $-\\frac{3}{5}=\\frac{(-3)}{5}.$\n\nTo raise the fraction to the power of $2$, we must raise both the numerator and the denominator to the power of $2:$\n\n$$\n{\\left(-\\frac{3}{5}\\right)}^{2}={\\left(\\frac{(-3)}{5}\\right)}^{2}=\\frac{(-3)^{2}}{{5}^{2}}\n$$\n\nNow, using $(-3)^{2}=9$ and ${5}^{2}=25,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{(-3)^{2}}{{5}^{2}}=\\frac{9}{25}.\n$$",
